4. ABOUT EMAIL SUBJECT TRICKS (NEW
   PATTERN)

  We have observed phishing with subject
  lines using Unicode bidirectional
  control characters (RLO, U+202E):
  the raw text reads backwards, but
  mail clients render it as a normal
  URL - "moc.epirts" displays as
  "stripe.com". If a subject line
  shows a URL, do not trust it:
  copy it to a text editor or view
  the raw headers to see the actual
  character order. Legitimate Stripe
  notifications never contain URLs
  in the subject line at all.

